{
  "description": "Broadcasts. Audiences became Segments and the spec marks `audience_id` deprecated; it is removed from createBroadcast and updateBroadcast, where `segment_id` replaces it, and kept in responses, which still carry it for older records. getBroadcast and sendBroadcast carry `object: \"broadcast\"` (live). Response members are narrowed to what Resend returns: required where resend-node, the maintained official SDK, declares them non-optional and every live response (2026-10-29) carried them, and nullable where resend-node allows null or a live response held null. A recipient's `count` and `clicked_links` stay optional: they appear only for the opened and clicked types. listBroadcastClickedLinks items (`id`, an opaque cursor, `url`, `clicks`, `unique_clicks`) match a real click on a delivery to a real mailbox. State errors match Resend's name, status and message, so they win over the generic class with the same name: a broadcast refuses edits, sends, deletes and cancels by status, and a sent broadcast can never be deleted. Errors on these operations match Resend's error `name` and status; the classes shared with other areas are in shared.json.",
